full_description:
Are you a graduate with a bachelor’s degree in automation, electromechanics or electricity? Do you feel capable of managing projects? Look no further, we have a great opportunity to offer you!  
For one of our clients active in HVAC in Belgium, we are looking for their next Software Engineer in the region across multiple sites.  
To do this, the Software Engineer will have to carry out the following tasks:  
- Program and optimize HVAC software (Siemens, PXC) within the framework of various projects;  
- Conduct on-site tests, solve technical problems, and support our teams in case of challenges;  
- Maintain smooth relations with our clients to ensure proper execution of projects and respect deadlines;  
- Document project follow-up, identify and resolve technical problems;  
- Actively collaborate with the project team to manage several HVAC installations in parallel on different sites.  
What we ask of you:  
- Bachelor’s degree in automation, electromechanics or electricity;  
- Minimum 3 years of experience in programming HVAC systems;  
- Mastery of Siemens software (Synco, S7, XWP, APT, TESigo CC) is a plus;  
- Ability to manage several projects simultaneously while respecting priorities;  
- Autonomy, initiative, and ability to work in a team;  
- Availability to work at clients’ premises and ability to adapt your hours.  
We offer you:  
- The opportunity to join a recognized company in Belgium with opportunities for growth at all levels;  
- Continuous training to update your skills and knowledge;  
- Flexible hours with telework options;  
- Full trust from day one with possible follow-up according to your needs and requests;  
- An attractive salary package with a computer, phone, and other social benefits;  
- Activities planned with teams throughout the year to maintain team spirit and good mutual understanding.  
APPLY TODAY!  
Apply on our website or contact us personally: 081/14.06.70 construct.wallonie.centre@actief.be 0471/61.94.07 (Whatsapp) Rue du Stordoir No. 67 - 5030 Gembloux (we can receive you every day from Monday to Friday from 08:30 to 12:30 and 13:30 to 17:30)  
Lara and Tamara will contact you within two working days!  
Are you looking for another job in the construction sector? We are recruiting in the regions of: Brussels Namur Walloon Brabant Luxembourg

Concretely, you:  
- provide expertise across all infrastructure components and provide expert-level technical support to operations teams, assisting them in reproducing, analyzing, diagnosing, and resolving incidents and problems;  
- analyze business or other Technology service needs and translate them into technical solutions;  
- propose and design technical solutions (and associated investments) and diagrams related to architecture, conduct technical studies, and act as a force of proposal regarding orientation and technical choices;  
- lead, with the IP networks team, the design of architecture, evolutions, and configuration in the following areas and technologies:  
  > LAN/WAN/WLAN, Access/Distribution/DataCenters, Media Networks (2110);  
  > Clouds and Virtualization;  
  > Security and monitoring;  
  > Essential services for IP networks: Load balancers, ADC, DNS/DHCP, Unified Communication;  
- participate in the procurement process: negotiate with suppliers (cost optimization), develop specifications, manage support contracts;  
- provide documentation, procedures, standards, and support change through communication and strong links with support;  
- manage/participate in various technical projects evolving the global architecture and contribute to the Architecture Committee;  
- show proactivity in technological watch and share new offerings from IP network technologies, applying these innovations to benefit the company;  
- ensure communication, coaching, and training of teams including operational and support teams and participate in organizing the team's work to guarantee coverage and optimal service.

a. To successfully carry out your missions, you have:  
- Expertise in physical and virtualized IP networks;  
- Expertise in IT architecture;  
- Mastery in IT security;  
- Knowledge of technical English;  
- Knowledge of TOGAF and Archimate tools/methods;  
- Knowledge in IT development (Scripting, IaC);  
- Knowledge in IT identities (Authentication, certificates/encryption, SSO, Firewalls, SIEM);  
- Knowledge in virtual platforms (and Microservices) and Cloud;  
- Knowledge of IP transmission techniques.

b. You possess the following skills:  
- Remain competent and efficient under stress, high pressure, or critical situations;  
- Take measures to stimulate your own personal and professional development;  
- Demonstrate a capacity to manage change;  
- Demonstrate good communication skills;  
- Adhere to and respect company values;  
- Build broad and effective relationship networks both inside and outside the organization;  
- Challenge the status quo and explore innovative paths;  
- Actively listen to colleagues to understand their motivations or resistances.

As a thematic advisor, develop strategic recommendations and participate in the definition of guidelines in the field in order to assist administrative and political bodies in their decision-making. Examples of tasks:  
- Reflect with others on the approach to the files, provide elements that may contribute to solutions, participate in brainstorming sessions on problems and files;  
- Participate in consultation meetings with members of the management committee, collaborators, and external stakeholders;  
- Write written opinions;  
- Develop strategic notes for the management committee.

As an analyst, perform analyses on the subject matter and related domains in order to formulate conclusions and decide on necessary actions. Examples of tasks:  
- Process and analyze collected data either to detect trends or make observations according to the initial request, to integrate the analysis into a broader project, or to conduct simulations or projections based on available data;  
- Reflect with others on the approach to files, provide elements that may contribute to solutions, participate in brainstorming sessions on problems and files;  
- Monitor national (and international) policy on the topic;  
- Analyze available statistics and publications (via the website, press releases, tables, analysis documents, etc.) and formulate proposals for potential improvements;  
- Manage projects within the framework of the objectives of the three-year strategic plan and the annual work plan.

