Introduction  
Do you want to use your commercial talent to make an impact and help build the future wind turbines in Belgium together with your team? Encon is looking for a  
Wind Energy Manager who leads a team of experts, capitalizes on commercial opportunities, and actively focuses on innovation. A role with responsibility, challenge, and the chance to truly shape the future of wind energy.  
As an expertise firm, Encon supports companies with innovative solutions during their transition to sustainability. Within our Wind Energy department, we have been realizing onshore wind projects from A to Z for over 15 years — from feasibility studies and permitting processes to engineering, procurement, and site supervision. Based on this expertise, the team also guides permitting applications for other sustainable energy installations such as large-scale solar parks and battery projects. Our Project Engineers & Project Managers apply their knowledge daily to accelerate the energy transition.  
To further strengthen our growth in the wind energy market, we are looking for a Wind Energy Manager. In this role, you will expand our market position, enlarge the project portfolio with strategic clients, and lead a team of professionals. You combine technical insight with entrepreneurship, stimulate innovation within the team, and know how to turn sustainable relationships with clients into commercial successes.  
Job description  
As a Wind Energy Manager, you hold ultimate responsibility for the commercial results, the department’s strategy, operational activities, and further team growth. You combine strategic insight with practical management. Your core tasks include:  
- Achieving commercial growth: you build a healthy and profitable project portfolio within the Belgian onshore wind market, thus strengthening Encon’s market position;  
- Securing new projects: you identify opportunities, develop convincing business cases and offers together with sales and marketing, and translate customer needs into concrete projects;  
- Strategic client management: you strengthen long-term strategic relationships with energy producers, project developers, governments, and industrial customers;  
- Operational management: you monitor progress, capacity, and quality of ongoing projects and adjust where necessary to achieve the expected results;  
- Team leadership: you inspire and coach a team of motivated Project Engineers, stimulate their professional growth, and create a positive, innovative work environment that reflects the Encon DNA;  
- Efficiency and knowledge safeguarding: you analyze and optimize existing processes, promote knowledge exchange, and ensure expertise retention within the team;  
- Stimulating innovation: you closely follow market trends and technological developments and translate these into innovative solutions and services within the wind energy sector;  
- Reporting: you report directly to the Business Unit Director Industry.

Your profile  
- You hold a master's degree in an economic or technical/economic field and have at least 10 years of experience in strategic project management, consultancy, or business development, preferably within the (sustainable) energy sector;  
- You have a proven track record in both commercial ultimate responsibility for a team and the successful execution of their projects. You are commercially sharp, recognize market opportunities, and know how to convert them into tangible results. You have experience leading teams and know how to motivate and develop people. You combine goal-oriented leadership with genuine attention and empathy for your team members;  
- You possess analytical insight and a hands-on mentality. You think ahead, dare to take initiative, and are comfortable with change;  
- You are a natural bridge-builder, actively seek collaboration, and create proper alignment both internally and externally;  
- You enjoy setting up complex projects with many stakeholders;  
- You have experience successfully managing relationships with (local) governments;  
- You communicate fluently in Dutch and English and know how to clearly, professionally, and convincingly present your ideas and proposals to clients and stakeholders.

About the job  
As an Innovation Consultant, you will be involved in the full range of PNO services, including EU grant applications, participation in EU funded projects where you will be leading activities related to stakeholders, market and business analysis and workshop organizations, and commercial consulting.  
Typical tasks include:  
- Writing of EU grant proposals while conceptualizing, visualizing and challenging the project ideas;  
- Active participation within EU funded projects with attention to starting up and the realization of official deliverables;  
- As such, you will actively be working on project planning, market and stakeholder analysis, workshop organization, business plan formulation and exploitation (and/or replication) strategy planning;  
- Execution of high-end innovation consulting services, especially for European Institutions, Technology Platforms, Sector Organizations and large corporate clients;  
- Expanding your network with potentially interesting partners;  
- Keeping yourself updated on the most important developments within your area of expertise.  
We have a hybrid working model, where you partly work from Zaventem (Brussels area) and partly from home office. You like to travel occasionally within Europe.

Responsibilities:
- You will dive into the development of our innovative digital platform, pushing the boundaries of what's possible in the semiconductor industry;
