-Based in Barcelona or surroundings | Subsidiary: Expert Pool Ibérica (Hexagone Sport Robotics Group) - Reporting to the Commercial Director Spain


---

- Robotics, service and sport: join the Hexagone movement

At Expert Pool Ibérica, the Spanish subsidiary of the French group Hexagone Sport Robotics, we design and market professional robotic solutions for the maintenance of public swimming pools, sports fields and sports pavilions.

More than selling machines, we help transform daily maintenance into a safer, more technical and more human experience. With more than 25,000 robots in operation in 35 countries, we are European leaders in autonomous sports robotics

YOUR MISSION

With a dual technical and commercial skillset, you will be the ambassador of our brand in Catalonia, with the following responsibilities:

Promote and sell our professional robots (pools, natural and synthetic grass, gyms);

Support clients in the public and private sectors: town halls, maintenance companies, sports centers, hotels, schools…;

Perform clear, quality, and educational demonstrations on site;

Carry out basic preventive maintenance and first-level technical assistance;

Actively participate in events, trade fairs and local presentations.

Your mission goes beyond selling: you will be a local reference for useful, ecological and efficient technology, with values of closeness and service.

---

PROFILE SOUGHT

Technical training or relevant experience in sales of professional equipment (mechanics, electricity, maintenance, machinery);

Ability to perform basic maintenance interventions (inspections, cleaning, simple diagnosis);

Ease of communication, autonomy, energy and customer sense;

Experience in sports facilities, swimming pools, gardening or municipal parks will be valued;

Languages: native Spanish, Catalan valued. To access the offer details click here

Description  
Attached to the Commercial division of KSB SAS, we are looking for our future Automation Unit Manager, a service that provides technical and commercial support to the sales teams in France for all Automation products in the broad sense (Pressure boosters, Variable speed drives, Control panels, Supervision products).  
In this capacity:  
- You hierarchically manage the team composed of 3 Sales Managers and 2 Order Managers;  
- Cross-functionally at the SAS level, you are the guarantor of the dynamic around Automation products for the sales forces; you participate in the technical training of the teams;  
- You are the preferred relay of the Commercial Management and participate in the development of Automation in the SAS revenue;  
- You perform reporting to the Commercial Director.  
- In daily tasks, you are a full member of the team and as such, you are led to directly manage files and/or after-sales requests.  

Profile  
