The proposed postdoctoral position aims to work on the development of a semi-distributed model at the scale of France using the Rameau calculation code developed at BRGM in connection with the MétéEAU Nappes platform. The idea is to develop a semi-automatic method to generate a mesh by sub-basin at the scale of France using a digital terrain model and according to the available hydrometric stations, then to calibrate the model according to flow records at these stations. A joint calibration will be carried out on piezometric level records selected by sub-basin. The goal is to have a tool at the scale of France that is as flexible as possible, adaptable – with variable geometry and easy addition of calibration data. The final aim is to obtain a model at the scale of France for seasonal forecasting aspects but also global changes in order to identify water resource evolution trends nationally.  

In parallel, innovative AI methods will be tested for the reproducibility of developed models and automatic calibration on a large number of observation points. Training techniques for models automatically from climatological time series will be implemented. Training methods by deep learning clustering, PINNS, etc. will be explored.  

Desired start date: 11/01/2025  
Contract type: Postdoctoral researcher  
Duration: 18 months  
Education: PhD  
Experience: 1 - 5 years  

You hold a doctorate for less than 3 years. You will need to mobilize the following skills and qualities:  
- Knowledge and practice of hydrological and/or hydrogeological modeling;  
- Experience in processing hydrometeorological time series;  
- Experience in programming and software development (Fortran 90, C++, Python, R);  
- Knowledge and practice of AI concepts (machine learning, deep learning, PINNS) and/or development of digital twins;  
- Interpersonal skills, team spirit, strong motivation, organization and rigor in: execution, reporting of work and compliance with contractual clauses;  
- Initiative and creativity;  
- Good oral and written communication skills to present scientific and technical project results (publications, articles, conference talks);  
- Mastery of English, written and oral.

